    Step 2 (applyMerge UPDATE branch — Q-DDD-1 fix): locate the current UPDATE branch (around line 55 of `drizzle-import-repository.ts` — the `if (existing) { await tx.update(gamesTable).set(values).where(...) }` block). REPLACE the shared inline `values` reference with a destructured insert-row:

      ```ts
      const insertRow = toGameInsertRow(userId, {
        kind: ng.kind,
        externalId: ng.externalId,
        title: ng.title,
        developer: ng.developer,
        genre: ng.genre,
        releaseYear: ng.releaseYear,
        platform: ng.platform,
        edition: ng.edition,
        hoursPlayed: ng.hoursPlayed,
        status: ng.status,
        format: ng.format,
        coverColor: ng.coverColor,
        coverImage: ng.coverImage,
        price: ng.price,
        purchasedAt: ng.purchasedAt,
        notes: ng.notes,
        metadataRef: ng.metadataRef
          ? {
              providerName: ng.metadataRef.providerName,
              providerId: ng.metadataRef.providerId,
              matchedAt: ng.metadataRef.matchedAt,
            }
          : null,
      });

      if (existing) {
        const { userId: _u, externalId: _e, kind: _k, createdAt: _c, updatedAt: _ua, ...updateSet } = insertRow;
        await tx
          .update(gamesTable)
          .set(updateSet)
          .where(and(eq(gamesTable.userId, userId), eq(gamesTable.id, existing.id)));
      } else {
        await tx.insert(gamesTable).values(insertRow);
      }
      ```

      Rationale: the INSERT and UPDATE paths in applyMerge encode the SAME snapshot-replay intent ("make the row look like this entry") — building `insertRow` once and stripping PK/timestamps for UPDATE is the 05-03 §5 pattern. Half-fixing only INSERT would mean a re-imported game silently keeps old cover/price/notes while a fresh-imported game gets the new values — asymmetric behavior keyed on row pre-existence. Worse than the original bug.

    Step 3 (applyReplace INSERT loop): mirror Step 1 in the applyReplace `for (const ng of plan.games)` loop. Identical 5-field append.

    Step 4: DO NOT touch DELETE block in applyReplace (D-29 + Q7 carve-out).
    Step 5: DO NOT change helper signature in schema.ts (already 18-field-capable).
    Step 6: DO NOT add new schema column.
    Step 7: DO NOT touch `DrizzleGameRepository.update()` or `saveMetadata()` — D-10 carve-out preserved (those are user-PATCH paths, not snapshot-replay).

    Run `bun run format apps/api/src/infrastructure/import/drizzle-import-repository.ts` and `bun run --filter=@apex/api typecheck`.
  </action>
