<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| ImportRepository.apply() input → DB writes | unchanged from 05-03: domain aggregates validated upstream |
| applyMerge INSERT branch + UPDATE branch + applyReplace INSERT loop → row payload | Q8 + Q-DDD-1 expansion: 18 columns persisted on INSERT; UPDATE branch destructure-and-update covers same 18 columns minus PK/timestamps |
| Round-trip export/import path (v4-carried fields only) | partial pin: invariant test in round-trip.test.ts covers `price`, `purchasedAt`, `notes`; `coverImage` + 3 metadata cols documented as BE-02c OPEN (blocked on v5) |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-5-09 | Silent data loss (Information Loss, not Disclosure) | applyMerge INSERT branch pre-Q8 | mitigate | Pre-Q8: 5 fields silently nulled on import. Post-Q8: full 18-field shape persisted on INSERT path. Pinned by apply-merge.test.ts Test 5. |
| T-5-09b | Silent data loss on row pre-existence (asymmetric — INSERT vs UPDATE) | applyMerge UPDATE branch — same function, same shared inline `values` block | mitigate | Q-DDD-1 fix: UPDATE branch uses destructure-and-update with same 18 fields minus PK/timestamps. Pinned by apply-merge.test.ts Test 7 (seed row with NULLs, merge with populated, assert update). |
| T-5-09c | Silent data loss on production import path (export drops fields, import omits propagation) | ImportData.execute + ExportSnapshotV4 schema | **accept (Phase 5) — flagged as BE-02c OPEN in CONCERNS.md** | Repo-layer fix (T-5-09, T-5-09b) is structurally inert on production path because v4 snapshot does not carry `coverImage` or `metadataRef`, so `g.coverImage` and `g.metadataRef` are `undefined` at the `ImportData.execute` NewGame.create call site. Mitigation deferred to future phase (ExportSnapshotV5). Discoverability: 3× `FIXME(BE-02c)` markers planted in `import-data.ts` + `export-snapshot.ts` (Task 4); CONCERNS Entry 7 OPEN with unblocking work list (Task 5 + 05-07 Task 1 coordination); round-trip test asserts `not.toHaveProperty(...)` to force a conscious decision when v5 adds the fields. |
| T-5-10 | Round-trip data drift (v4-scoped) | snapshot ↔ import path | mitigate (partially — v4 scope) | round-trip.test.ts Test 1 diffs snapshot1 vs snapshot2 (modulo auto-PK/timestamps) through real `ImportData.execute` use-case. Catches future regressions in v4-carried fields. Outside v4 scope: see T-5-09c. |
| T-5-11 | Per-user data leak via export query (IDOR regression vector in `exportSnapshot` userId predicate) | export-snapshot.ts | mitigate | round-trip.test.ts Test 3 seeds TEST_USER_A (3 games) + TEST_USER_B (2 games), asserts `exportSnapshot(TEST_USER_A).games.length === 3`. A regressed userId predicate would return 5 → test fails red. |
| T-5-03 | Information Disclosure (IDOR) | applyMerge/applyReplace batched SELECT | accept (unchanged from 05-03) | Q8 + Q-DDD-1 only expand the column-set passed to `.values()` and `.set()`; WHERE predicates and batched SELECTs are untouched. Per-user scoping preserved by virtue of NOT touching the WHERE clauses. |
</threat_model>

